# STRICT ARCHITECTURAL IMMUTABILITY & ANTI-REGRESSION RULES
1. IMMUTABILITY CONTRACT: NEVER delete, rename, or change the method signature of existing public methods, events, properties, or fields in any file.
2. SURGICAL ADDITIONS ONLY: When adding a new feature, append new isolated modular methods, helper classes, or subscribe to the OmniEventBus. Do NOT refactor working methods unless explicitly instructed with a targeted diff.
3. OUTPUT FORMAT: Output ONLY the complete, syntactically verified code block for the single target file. Zero conversational filler, zero markdown explanations.
4. DEPENDENCY RULE: Features must communicate exclusively through `Assets/Scripts/Core/IOmniEvents.cs` or explicit C# interfaces. No direct circular tight-coupling.
5. MEMORY & TOKEN LOCK: Never read or index directories outside the immediate target file context.
